<title>CANADA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>CANADA GOVERNMENT LIST (970427)</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p>  *  2 Jun 97 - General elections to be held.		   *</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************  Governor General (Took office 8 Feb 95).........Romeo LEBLANC</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>LIBERAL PARTY GOVERNMENT</p>
<p> (Formed 4 Nov 93, Reshuffled 4 Oct 96)</p>
<p> Prime Minister (Sworn in 4 Nov 93)..............Jean CHRETIEN</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister.............Sheila COPPS</p>
<p> (Also Minister of Canadian Heritage)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture.......Ralph GOODALE</p>
<p> Canadian Heritage....See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p> Citizenship &amp; Immigration...Lucienne ROBILLARD</p>
<p> Defence &amp; Veterans Affairs.......Douglas YOUNG</p>
<p> Environment.......Sergio MARCHI</p>
<p> Finance.............Paul MARTIN</p>
<p> Fisheries &amp; Oceans................Fred MIFFLIN</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs..Lloyd AXWORTHY</p>
<p> Health...........David DINGWALL</p>
<p> Human Resources Development</p>
<p>    (Social Programs)..........Pierre PETTIGREW</p>
<p> Indian Affairs &amp; Northern Development...............Ron IRWIN</p>
<p> Industry............John MANLEY</p>
<p> International Co-operation &amp; Francophonie.........Don BOUDRIA</p>
<p> International Trade...............Art EGGLETON</p>
<p> Justice, Attorney General...........Allan ROCK</p>
<p> Labour.........Alfonso GAGLIANO</p>
<p> (Also Deputy Government Leader in the House of Commons)  Literacy........Joyce FAIRBAIRN</p>
<p> (Also Government Leader in the Senate)  National Revenue...Jane STEWART</p>
<p> Natural Resources (Energy).......Anne MCLELLAN</p>
<p> President of Privy Council, Intergovernmental</p>
<p>    Affairs........Stephane DION</p>
<p> Public Works &amp; Government Services..............Diane MARLEAU</p>
<p> Solicitor General.....Herb GRAY</p>
<p> (Also Government leader in the House of Commons)  Transport........David ANDERSON</p>
<p> Treasury Board.....Marcel MASSE</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor..........Gordon THIESSEN</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
